# XINC1 - havok continuous simulation: the probe step 0x00d100a0 calls the placed 0x00d0f300. Method: docs/PATCHES.md.

@@ XINC1 src/havok/physics/dynamics/world/simulation/continuous/hkpcontinuoussimulation.cpp 0x00d100a0
# x86 0x00d100a0 reaches 0x00d0f300 with `call 0x00d0f300` and eight stack words, cdecl: the caller pops them itself
# (0x20 bytes, folded into the `add esp` after the next call), ecx is not set for it, and the callee ends in a plain
# `ret`. Push order, first to last: the probe's query block, the solver state, the event pair (its own argument),
# the phase object (the simulation's member at +0x48, passed as a pointer), the world argument, the active-entity
# array, the flag view, and the rotation float (the caller's last argument, stored into the slot the previous cdecl
# call's first word had used). The callee reads the event pair at its third word and the float at its eighth, and
# never calls the solver-step finisher after the violation handling, which the second, unplaced rendering of the
# unit (invented helper names) does. That rendering is not the exe function; the placed definition of 0x00d0f300 is.
# The call takes the placed definition's reference types by cast: the same eight words, so MSVC pushes the same
# addresses and calls the same address, and the unplaced overload has no caller left.
<<<
int result=FUN_00d0f300(query,state,event,*m_arr30.m_phase,world,active,flags,rotation);
===
int result=FUN_00d0f300((const Limits&)query,(Resources&)state,(PairEvent&)event,(ResourceManager&)*m_arr30.m_phase,(Scene*)world,(List<DynamicNode*>&)active,(StateTable&)flags,rotation);
>>>

@@ XINC1 src/havok/physics/dynamics/world/simulation/continuous/hkpcontinuoussimulation.cpp 0x00d0d020
# The unplaced rendering of 0x00d0f300 (the overload taking EventQuery, SolverState, ...; it calls the invented
# finishSolveStep / backstepSolveBody / updateSolveTransform / projectSolveTransform) is not an exe function: the exe
# has exactly one call of 0x00d0f300, at 0x00d102bc in 0x00d100a0 (no other call, jmp or address word anywhere in
# .text), and the site above makes it call the placed definition. The overload has no caller left, no exe address
# and its four callees are declared only, so the object kept dead code in .text (one section per unit, no
# gc-sections possible) whose relocations were four undefined names, i.e. four trap stubs in the guest. `static`
# makes it an internal function nothing calls: GCC drops it, MSVC emits no code for an unreferenced static one.
<<<
int __cdecl FUN_00d0f300(const EventQuery&,SolverState&,Entry70&,PhaseObj&,Arg0*,PtrArr&,SolverFlagView&,float);
===
static int __cdecl FUN_00d0f300(const EventQuery&,SolverState&,Entry70&,PhaseObj&,Arg0*,PtrArr&,SolverFlagView&,float);
>>>
<<<
__declspec(noinline) int __cdecl FUN_00d0f300(const EventQuery& query,
===
static __declspec(noinline) int __cdecl FUN_00d0f300(const EventQuery& query,
>>>

@@ XINC1 src/havok/physics/dynamics/world/simulation/continuous/hkpcontinuoussimulation_rtm_variant.cpp file
# Same as the main unit: the variant defines the unplaced overload of 0x00d0f300 and has no caller of it (no
# 0x00d100a0 definition; the exe's only call of 0x00d0f300 is at 0x00d102bc). Made static, it is dropped, and
# finishSolveStep / backstepSolveBody / updateSolveTransform / projectSolveTransform are no longer referenced.
<<<
int __cdecl FUN_00d0f300(const EventQuery&,SolverState&,Entry70&,PhaseObj&,Arg0*,PtrArr&,SolverFlagView&,float);
===
static int __cdecl FUN_00d0f300(const EventQuery&,SolverState&,Entry70&,PhaseObj&,Arg0*,PtrArr&,SolverFlagView&,float);
>>>
<<<
__declspec(noinline) int __cdecl FUN_00d0f300(const EventQuery& query,
===
static __declspec(noinline) int __cdecl FUN_00d0f300(const EventQuery& query,
>>>
